1
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,352
NARRATOR : For weeks , rumours have spread across Mars .

2
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:27,553
From outposts to settlements , from town to town .

3
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:32,113
Something that had been buried for centuries has just been uncovered .

4
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:36,957
And , as this mysterious force moves across the Southern valley ,

5
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,751
it leaves behind only silence and death .

6
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,430
Take your seats , please .

7
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,392
I just talked with the Cartel .

8
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:49,696
They 're concerned that the rumours are getting out of control .

9
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,234
They 'd like to make a statement in two hours .

10
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:55,673
Some of you may not know we 've had another incident .

11
00:02:55,760 --> 00:03:00,277
At 15 : 20 yesterday a freight train , Trans Marineris 74 Yankee ,

12
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:03,751
returned from the southern valley on auto pilot .

13
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:06,719
SECURITY OFFICER : Get to your security stations now !

14
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,439
Okay , let 's move !

15
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:27,633
INQUISITOR : Initial reports indicated it was a ghost train .

16
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:29,512
It appeared no-one was aboard

17
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:33,070
until a single survivor was discovered in a rear compartment .

18
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:34,912
OFFICER : Call for Med-Tech backup .

19
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,116
INQUISITOR : Lieutenant Melanie Ballard .

20
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:40,153
Second Officer for a squad of escort police .

21
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,470
They were assigned to transfer a prisoner

22
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:45,313
from the jail at Shining Canyon mine back here to Chryse .

23
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:49,559
Lieutenant Ballard was taken to hospital under guard .

24
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:53,670
She had superficial wounds but was in otherwise good physical condition .

25
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:57,555
However , traces of an illegal substance , tetromonochloride ,

26
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:59,233
were found in her system .

27
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,755
MEDIC : It 's gonna be all right . Take it easy .

28
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,989
Bring her in , please .

29
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,276
INQUISITOR : Lieutenant Ballard , please be seated .

30
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:22,676
Do I get a lawyer , or don 't police officers have rights these days ?

31
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:26,191
Representation by counsel won 't be necessary .

32
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:29,233
Your rights are protected by the Matronage .

33
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,833
You can speak freely .

34
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:33,679
- Then I 'm not being charged ? - Sit down , Lieutenant .

35
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:38,152
This is a discovery hearing , and your presence is required as ranking officer .

36
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,670
I want your ' After Action ' report .

37
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,992
Where 's the rest of your team ? The prisoner you were sent to pick up ?

38
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:46,396
What happened at Shining Canyon ?

39
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:52,436
Last Friday at 17 : 50 , we were slamming through a dust storm

40
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:55,075
on the edge of the southern valley .

41
00:04:56,280 --> 00:05:00,672
74 Yankee was an ore hauler servicing the mines in the outer sector .

42
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:04,997
My squad was hitching a ride into Shining Canyon .

43
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:07,636
JERICHO : Hmm , you beat me .

44
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:10,599
You 've played Tarts before . Nah , I 've never done this .

45
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:14,153
JERICHO : Let 's spin ' em again . One down and one up .

46
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:16,317
( TAPPING CARDS )

47
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,997
Fuck me , the Five of Bats .

48
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:23,515
You 've got the Wheeler . What 's your wager ?

49
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:25,594
Five bucks .

50
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,197
Helena . Hey ...

51
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,597
Sorry .

52
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:39,433
Weather station 's tracking a huge storm across the southern sector

53
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:41,431
and we 're right under it by now .

54
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:45,829
What 's the mark on it ?

55
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:49,351
3200 kicks . We should be there by 18 : 00 .

56
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:57,478
So , erm , just let me know if you need anything .

57
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:48,670
BRADDOCK : Melanie !

58
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,999
You high ?

59
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:54,037
Fuck , Helena , it 's just Clear .

60
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:57,279
I 'll be straighter than this track line before we hit the canyon .

61
00:06:57,440 --> 00:07:00,751
Well , you better be . This prisoner transfer is no sleepwalk .

62
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,439
We 're picking up James Williams .

63
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:04,678
You mean ' Desolation ' Williams ?

64
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:09,271
Cooling his heels in the Shining Canyon jail . Deep solitary .

65
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:13,196
What 's the charge this time ? Murder .

66
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:17,270
Man 's been up on murder three times . He gets off every time in self defence .

67
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:20,113
It 's different this time . Sounds like he finally went psycho .

68
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,390
Beaucoup corpses , all mutilated .

69
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:26,756
Williams shows up at Shining Canyon mine with some bizarre-ass story .

70
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:30,430
Sends three officers to the medevac before they locked him down .

71
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,999
You startin ' to see the picture ?

72
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:36,593
And all we got is you , me , this new guy , Jericho , and a couple of rookies ?

73
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,956
BRADDOCK : What do you think of Sergeant Jericho ?

74
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:42,436
I mean , I was hoping we 'd get a good , solid woman we could count on .

75
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,710
BALLARD : I don 't know . I guess we 'll see .

76
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:47,678
Well ...

77
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:50,511
I need you straight , Melanie .

78
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:58,312
Don 't worry about that , Commander . I 'm as straight as they come .

79
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,557
Such a shame .

80
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:05,677
Check on our transfer schedule .

81
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:09,120
McSIMMS : Shining Canyon .

82
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:12,716
Shining Canyon , this is Trans Marineris 74 Yankee .

83
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:14,719
They ready for us ?

84
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:17,838
This storm 's really kicking up a mess . I can 't get through to the tower .

85
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:21,595
Here 's your coffee , Mr. McSimms , three sugars , two whites , the way you like it .

86
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:24,069
You want some ? No , thanks .

87
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:26,231
How long ?

88
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:28,197
About 40 .

89
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,191
Shining Canyon ?

90
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:32,914
Shining Canyon , this is Trans Marineris 74 Yankee .

91
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:35,270
ETA 40 minutes .

92
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:39,312
Everybody check your equipment . I don 't want any surprises .

93
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:44,315
Is everything all right , Lieutenant ?

94
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:48,435
I couldn 't help but notice that charming scene with the Queen Bee .

95
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:50,875
Yeah , well you know how the service is , Sergeant .

96
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:54,510
She figures if I want to make Captain , I 'll have to pay the price .

97
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:57,274
Thing is , I don 't give a damn about wearing another bar .

98
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,158
Yeah , it could be that .

99
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,960
Or maybe she has good taste in women .

100
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:05,393
Sergeant , you are seriously out of line .

101
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:07,756
I 'd hate to spoil my record .

102
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:08,840
All right !

103
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:12,599
I know you think you 're some pretty tough hombres .

104
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:16,951
You 've had the best training , you have the best gear .

105
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:19,953
You probably think this is a routine prisoner transfer .

106
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,776
But that 's what I want to bang into your heads ,

107
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:24,155
there 's nothing routine about this prisoner .

108
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:27,631
We 're here to pick up James Desolation ' Williams .

109
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:30,434
I want y 'all jack-ready and double-tough .

110
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:55,720
Officers , you can disembark here .

111
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:57,669
What time 's departure ?

112
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,920
We need at least a half an hour to secure our prisoner .

113
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:04,193
We got about a four-hour turnaround , and we 're due back at this spot at about

114
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:07,113
22 : 00 . You can report anytime after that .

115
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,510
See if you can raise the Yard Master , will ya ?

116
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:11,955
Ed ?

117
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,474
Ed , you out there ?

118
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,318
Rookies , use your breathers .

119
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:18,950
We not gonna have air like Earth for 10 more years . Let 's go .

120
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:46,031
BASHIRA : God , I hate this thing . BRADDOCK : You 'll get used to it .

121
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:49,636
Two years ago we were sill wearing full-face breathers .

122
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:53,600
BALLARD : Takes about a month to get over the headaches out here .

123
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:57,594
BASHIRA : So this is Shining Canyon ? God , what a dump !

124
00:10:57,840 --> 00:11:00,912
BALLARD : First time in the boonies , rookie ? JERICHO : Standard layout .

125
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,389
Just another shitty boomtown like all the others .

126
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:05,039
Seen one you can go home .

127
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:07,216
BALLARD : You 're always cold , you can 't get a decent shower ,

128
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,356
and they don 't tell you that a one-year contract here

129
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:11,830
equals two years , Earth time .

130
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:14,232
Gotta read the fine print .

131
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,639
JERICHO : Where is everybody ?

132
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:25,955
Yeah , Friday night , the place should be packed .

133
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:29,673
I mean , a whole 12 hours before sun-up , and there 's money to bum ,

134
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:32,673
whores to fuck and drugs to take .

135
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:35,920
Instead we got a graveyard .

136
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:40,352
Maybe they 're all inside spending their money .

137
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:42,511
I 'm gonna get us squared away at the rec-fac .

138
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:45,035
You and Sergeant Jericho go check in at the jail .

139
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,230
BALLARD : Save some hot water for me .

140
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:53,830
Where were you before Chryse ?

141
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:55,752
Utopia .

142
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:58,629
It 's the arse end of the universe .

143
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:02,111
A penal camp full of work-amnesty cutthroats .

144
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,878
Sounds nasty .

145
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:06,793
But you seem to be holding together all right .

146
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:08,871
What you see is nothing .

147
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,676
I have numerous hidden talents .

148
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,839
Need some help with that ?

149
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,358
You 're persistent , aren 't you ?

150
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:35,551
I 've changed a few minds in my time .

151
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:38,880
There 's not many of us breeders around .

152
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,440
I 'd hate to miss a chance to give it a go .

153
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,358
What do you say ?

154
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:46,431
( DOOR OPENS )

155
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:55,076
Hello !

156
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:58,155
Anybody here ?

157
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:16,832
- ( FEEDBACK SCREECH ) - Officer to front desk .

158
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:29,793
Well , hello Mr. Williams .

159
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:36,475
No-one seems to be about . What do you make of it ?

160
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:37,715
I don 't know .

161
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:40,156
Do you want me to pop the lock and ask the prisoners ?

162
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:43,000
What do you mean " pop the lock " ? That 's a level-8 security door .

163
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:47,357
I 've got a mystical way with locks and mechanical objects .

164
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:49,756
There isn 't machine on Mars that doesn 't love me .

165
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:53,599
How about we check with the commander first ?

166
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:59,150
So , what do you do for fun , then ?

167
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:02,949
Are you a gambler ? No , I 'm short-time , Sergeant .

168
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,635
I believe in saving my money .

169
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:08,638
Don 't worry about that .

170
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:10,956
I was gonna do it for free .

171
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,678
Let me put it this way :

172
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:16,600
Maybe I 'd sleep with you if you were the last man on Earth .

173
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:22,159
- But we 're not on Earth . - ( MUFFLED EXPLOSION )

174
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:26,634
JERICHO : That 's a voltage overload , most likely .

175
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:29,356
Wanna check it out ?

176
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:32,160
It 's probably nothing .

177
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:35,552
But , on second thought ...

178
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,349
Police officer . Anybody there ?

179
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,513
Oh , shit !

180
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,591
Jericho !

181
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,517
( SLICING SOUND )

182
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:10,318
- This is not making me happy . - All right , it 's time to get back-up .

183
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:43,913
Jesus Christ !

184
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:45,873
What are you doing ?

185
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:48,399
I almost killed you .

186
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:52,550
- What 's going on ? - Rec-fac 's a slaughterhouse .

187
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:54,514
What ?

188
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,229
" Slaughterhouse " ?

189
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:59,396
That 's the word Descanso used .

190
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:01,557
I didn 't see it myself .

191
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,680
According to what Commander Braddock told me

192
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:06,189
right after we first arrived in Shining Canyon ,

193
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:09,511
she and the two rookies headed towards the recreation facility .

194
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,431
I 'm gonna get us squared away at the rec-fac .

195
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:15,273
You and Sergeant Jericho go check in at the jail .

196
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:18,040
BALLARD : Save some hot water for me .

197
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:24,598
( WIND HOWLING )

198
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:42,911
Descanso , sweep left .

199
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:47,229
Bashira , stick with me .

200
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:50,714
Bashira !

201
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:52,639
Bashira !

202
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:04,996
- ( RADIO WHISTLING ) - Officer to train , do you read ?

203
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:08,080
The casino , the barracks , the dining hall , the rec centre ...

204
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,349
No-one alive anywhere !

205
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:13,110
Commander .

206
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,395
What ?

207
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:18,233
I can 't reach the train .

208
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,274
Well , keep trying .

209
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:25,239
Whaddya think , how we doing ?

210
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,471
I dunno . This was built to stay locked .

211
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:30,677
And Williams is still locked up ?

212
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:32,875
What do you mean ?

213
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:37,877
He was arrested on suspicion of murdering six rail workers and a payroll courier

214
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,758
up at klick 305 Hub Station .

215
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:43,515
The bodies were hung and decapitated , just like the bodies found in the rec-fac .

216
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:49,029
- So how 'd they pin that on ' Desolation ' ? - He showed up with the courier 's payroll .

217
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:53,393
The cashier realised it was stolen scrip , they made their arrest .

218
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:55,357
There 's gotta be a day log here somewhere .

219
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:58,435
Sergeant 's desk .

220
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:06,191
( RADIO NOISE )

221
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,315
Here .

222
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:15,160
" Last night the mine called in a work stoppage .

223
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:18,480
" Reported winds gusting up to 60 knots . "

224
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,471
- 60 ? - That 's what it says .

225
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,554
Anything else ?

226
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:25,638
" Arrested for theft " Then nothing .

227
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:28,314
( ELECTRONIC LOCK WHIRRING ) Got it .

228
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,958
What the hell 's going on around here ?

229
00:19:57,040 --> 00:20:00,510
We haven 't had a meal or a piss break in six hours .

230
00:20:01,040 --> 00:20:02,917
Descanso , open the door .

231
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,560
All right , everybody , answer " here " when I call your name .

232
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:07,114
- Akooshay . - What ?

233
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:10,000
- Just answer " here " . - Here .

234
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,515
- Zimmerman . - I 'm right in front of you .

235
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:13,830
Benchley .

236
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:16,840
Who 's that ?

237
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,160
AKOOSHAY : She showed up last night .

238
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:21,115
Checked herself in .

239
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:23,715
Insisted on being locked up here with us .

240
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:25,711
Well , wake her up , sunshine .

241
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:27,831
Let 's hear what she has to say .

242
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:30,679
Hey ! Hey !

243
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:32,996
Somebody wants to talk to you .

244
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:37,033
Who are you ? Whit lock .

245
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:39,720
What are you doing in the holding tank , Whit lock ?

246
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:44,073
It 's the only safe place at the moment , okay ?

247
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:46,310
Can I go back to sleep now ? No , you can 't .

248
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:48,033
I need answers .

249
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:49,878
What 's going on out there ?

250
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,514
What 's your ID ?

251
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:58,592
Dr. Arlene Whit lock .

